    <string name="about_app">Reverb · 余音</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version 1.0.0</string>
    <string name="about_h_what">What is this</string>
    <string name="about_p_what">Reverb is a lightweight podcast client with an ink-and-wash aesthetic. Discover shows, subscribe, download for offline, and resume anytime — focused on listening.</string>
    <string name="about_h_features">Features</string>
    <string name="about_p_features">· Discover: browse daily charts by region and category; reorder and swipe between categories\n· Search: by name or paste an RSS URL\n· Library: manage Subscriptions, Downloads and History\n· Offline downloads: cache while listening, Wi-Fi-only optional\n· Playback: speed, skip, sleep timer, resume, background &amp; lock-screen controls\n· Show notes: swipe on the player\n· New-episode notifications\n· Appearance: dark/light/system, text size, accent color, multiple languages</string>
    <string name="about_h_philosophy">Design</string>
    <string name="about_p_philosophy">Visually it draws on ink, celadon and beam-gold — the name and icon echo “an echo circling the rafters.”\n\nFor sources it stays entirely free, no login, no API key: it searches open directories like Apple, fyyd and gpodder, then always returns to the publisher\'s own RSS and streams the original audio — copyright-clean, zero cost.\n\nFor privacy, subscriptions, history and downloads live only on your device — never uploaded, never tracked.</string>

    <string name="licenses_title">Open-source licenses</string>
    <string name="licenses_intro">Reverb is built with the following open-source software, with thanks.</string>
    <string name="licenses_h_libs">Libraries</string>
    <string name="licenses_h_sources">Data sources</string>
    <string name="licenses_sources_note">These are public podcast directory/search APIs, used only for search and charts; audio always comes from the publisher\'s original RSS. This app never re-hosts or proxies it.</string>

